# Phase 3 live data sources.
#
# FRED (src/proxy/crude_proxy.py) needs NO key -- its CSV endpoint
# (fredgraph.csv) is public. Nothing to put here for it.
#
# API Ninjas and OilPriceAPI.com both offer a genuinely free, no-credit-card
# tier with better-than-monthly granularity (confirmed by reading their own
# docs during Phase 3) -- but both require an account signup to issue an API
# key, which this project's automation does not do on your behalf. If you
# want to use either, sign up yourself, then set the key below and wire it
# into src/proxy/crude_proxy.py (not done yet -- FRED is the only source
# actually integrated as of Phase 3).
#
# API_NINJAS_KEY=
# OILPRICEAPI_KEY=

# Phase 4: Supabase (public dashboard + weekly automation).
#
# SUPABASE_DB_URL is the direct Postgres "Connection string" (URI form,
# password filled in) from Supabase project Settings -> Database ->
# Connection string. Used ONLY by scripts/sync_to_supabase.py, which runs
# in GitHub Actions (as a repo secret), never in the browser. This is
# different from the anon/public key baked into docs/index.html's
# client-side JS -- that one is meant to be public (see supabase/schema.sql's
# RLS policies), this one is not.
#
# SUPABASE_DB_URL=postgresql://postgres:[PASSWORD]@db.[PROJECT-REF].supabase.co:5432/postgres

# Optional: weekly email alert (scripts/send_alert_email.py). Use a Gmail
# "App Password" (Google Account -> Security -> 2-Step Verification ->
# App passwords), NOT your real Gmail password -- an app password can be
# revoked independently and has no access beyond SMTP send.
#
# ALERT_EMAIL_FROM=your-gmail-address@gmail.com
# ALERT_EMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=
# ALERT_EMAIL_TO=lycinremy@gmail.com
